  data: {
    LLM: "Save your matching cards for when you have a breakaway. Playing a Jack is the easiest way to enter a scoring position.\n\nTrack which ranks have been played. If many 8s are gone, an 8 is a 'safer' card to play when your opponent has a breakaway because it's harder for them to match it.\n\nTactical card management: Lead with cards you have pairs for in your hand, so you can immediately 'score' if your opponent matches your lead.",
